{"name":"Detective Thriller","hex":"#393c40","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"detective","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A police officer tasked with collecting evidence and information in order to solve a crime; an investigator.","A person employed to find information not otherwise available to the public."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Employed in detecting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detective"},{"term":"thriller","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that thrills.","A suspenseful, sensational genre of story, book, play, film."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thriller"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thriller (genre)","blocks":[{"text":"Thriller is a genre of fiction with numerous, often overlapping, subgenres, including crime, horror, and detective fiction. Thrillers are characterized and defined by the moods they elicit, giving their audiences heightened feelings of suspense, excitement, surprise, anticipation and anxiety. This genre is well suited for making thriller films and television programs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Hitchcock_Hedren_Marnie_Publicity_Photo.jpg/330px-Hitchcock_Hedren_Marnie_Publicity_Photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thriller_(genre)","wikidata":"Q182015"},{"title":"Detective","blocks":[{"text":"A detective is an investigator, usually a member of a law enforcement agency. They often collect information to solve crimes by talking to witnesses and informants, collecting physical evidence, or searching records in databases. This leads them to arrest criminals and enable them to be convicted in court. A detective may work for the police or privately."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Oklahoma_City_Police_Homicide_Detectives.jpeg/330px-Oklahoma_City_Police_Homicide_Detectives.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detective","wikidata":"Q842782"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Leman_Street_detectives.jpg/330px-Leman_Street_detectives.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Leman_Street_detectives.jpg/330px-Leman_Street_detectives.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"H Division, of police detectives, including Frederick Abberline (left, with cane), at Leman Street police station, of the London Metropolitan Police, two years before the Jack the Ripper serial killer murders of 1888. Photograph circa 1886","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeman_Street_detectives.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg/500px-Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg/1280px-Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg/500px-Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Allan Pinkerton (pictured here circa 1861) was, in 1850, a detective of the Chicago Police Department and, in 1851, the founder of the Pinkerton Detective Agency.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAllan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Edward_Bonney.jpg/250px-Edward_Bonney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d3/Edward_Bonney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=